codex
I’m going to add a materialized final-gate path: one Triton kernel will normalize the hidden update and write a contiguous fp16 `[rows, 128]` buffer, then cuBLAS will do the final `128 -> dim` projection. This trades one extra write for a much faster dense projection on dim-384 cases.
